SUMMARY:[Digital Economy Lab] Neil Thompson: Forecasting AI’s Impact on 
 Human Expertise and the Future of Work
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T130000
DTSTAMP:20261009T184050Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54100806959750-54100806960775@local-events
DESCRIPTION:AI is advancing rapidly at the cognitive tasks that make up kn
 owledge work\, raising fears among firms\, policymakers\, and\, not least
 \, workers of a “China shock” for white-collar jobs. Neil Thompson wil
 l present new research on whether those fears are warranted. The research 
 asks which tasks AI will take over and what that means for the expertise r
 equired in the work that remains. The time a skilled person needs for a ta
 sk strongly predicts whether AI can do it\, and AI is handling ever-longer
  task\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/event
 /neil-thompson-seminar-series/\nLast synced: 2026-10-09 11:40 PDT
LOCATION:Gates Computer Science Building
URL:https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/event/neil-thompson-seminar-series
 /
END:VEVENT
